        <h3>
        A Global Pathway to Net Zero Buildings:
        A Correlation Network Analysis of Building Information Modelling (BIM)-based Whole Life Carbon Assessment Challenges
        </h3>

        <p>
        Achieving net zero buildings requires better decisions, not only better technologies.
        This project introduces "builtenv-cna", an open-source analytical framework,
        which transforms 145 empirical questionnaire survey responses into correlation networks
        for system-level analysis.

        Findings from this study motivates the upcoming development of human-AI decision systems 
        that can support trustworthy sustainable decision-making in buildings and cities.
        </p>

