    <h3>Disrupting the Undisruptable: Agentic AI Innovations in Construction</h3>

    <p>
    Agentic AI is reshaping innovation processes across
    industries. However, socially impactful industries such as construction, healthcare, and
    education remain resistant to technological changes. Grounded in the Disruptive Innovation
    Theory coined by Harvard Professor Clayton Christensen, this study explores how agentic AI challenges and reshapes innovation
    dynamics in the construction industry: a sector characterised by slow technological
    adoption, complex institutional constraints, and fragmented project structures.
    </p>

